{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — computed properties, "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-four-rules","text":"The four rules","level":2},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"computed property \/ expression","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@GestureState"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.drag"},{"type":"text","text":" — Drag"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (helper)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(.spring)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".transition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier — that’s a different concept).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","text":"Pure value patch → computed property","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Add","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition\/interpolate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","text":"Flag, don’t fake","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimapping